    "body": "Modified this PR to load the `html-dfn` and `commit-snapshot-shortcut-key` scripts as `defer`. Keeping their `DOMContentLoaded` listeners as they are. It's now guaranteed that the scripts are run, and the listeners added, before the `DOMContentLoaded` actually fires.\r\n\r\nFor other scripts, it makes sense to be `async`, we don't need to load them all the same way. For example, the `file-issue` load strategy was changed in #2024 in the other direction, from `defer` to `async`. Because it inserts an absolutely-positioned \"File an issue\" link, and it's preferrable to see that link ASAP, long before the huge one-page version of the document fully parses and loads.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
