    "created_at": "2023-05-30T08:53:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-30T08:53:25Z",
    "body": "Hi @annevk :wave: the contributor agreement has been signed on behalf of the entire Automattic organization, I think we can proceed with this now.\r\n\r\nAnd while I have your attention, there's one question about `defer` and `async` that bugs me. The HTML standard specifies how `defer` and `async` script loading interacts with parsing and the `DOMContentLoaded` and `load` events, but are there any constraints that would specify relations with rendering and painting?\r\n\r\nNowadays we have metrics like First Contentful Paint, they are considered very important, but it's possible, both theoretically and in practice, that a `defer` or `async` script significantly delays the FCP, although it wouldn't have to. Executing a script \"as soon as possible\" can mean that it's executed at a time when there's already a \"rendering opportunity\", and the script execution is delaying that oportunity.\r\n\r\nHas this ever been discussed anywhere?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1568034271/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
